abstract: >-
  A deterministic, observer-centred dataset for the Solar System N-body problem.
  The Sun receives a single forward-only stream of light-delayed echoes from the
  eight planets (46,786 events over 88.4 days; 4.7 million over 25 years), each
  carrying a Compton-frequency source signature, a 1/r^2 return amplitude and a
  direction, with no positions or planet labels exposed. Planet positions come
  from JPL approximate Keplerian elements (1800-2050) propagated as isolated
  two-body ellipses, so planet-planet interaction enters only as secular element
  drift. The stream is intended as input for testing whether Structured
  Knowledge Accumulation can infer relational structure (W_ij) without an
  assumed force law.